## THE FINDING AND WHAT THE FIX ASKS (source: gate B1647 VERDICT `/Volumes/Datasec_DEV/TUESDAY/2_Project_Files/tuesday/briefs/2026-11-16_B1647_verify/VERDICT.md`, section F1, RELAYED: read it whole at Step 0; RE-PROVED at `ed3b1aed` by the drafter, below)
- **Gate F1 (measured over HTTP at `dcac002d` and the storage-family head):** sign-in enforced, NO stored authorized user, cookie `session_token=__proto__`, `constructor` or `toString`: 200 on `/api/auth/check` (`authenticated:true,user:null`), `/api/printers`, `/api/stats`, POST `/api/chat`; 403 on the admin `/api/auth/users`; `prototype` 401. With ONE stored user: 500 `AUTH_ERROR` on every route. The storage-family slice removed only the half that wrote `lastActivity` onto built-ins.
- **RE-PROVED AT MAIN `ed3b1aed` (MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER, the defect still exists).** (i) In-process: `probe/p_getsession.js` in the drafter's scratch `/Volumes/Datasec_DEV/TUESDAY/2_Project_Files/fleet/state/s285/b1657/`, node v26.13.0, the `backend/` tree of a tarball export of `ed3b1aed`, `HOME` and `DATA_DIR` set to a fresh scratch folder BEFORE the require, no server: `Object.getOwnPropertyNames(Object.prototype)` has **12** names (`constructor`, `__defineGetter__`, `__defineSetter__`, `hasOwnProperty`, `__lookupGetter__`, `__lookupSetter__`, `isPrototypeOf`, `propertyIsEnumerable`, `toString`, `valueOf`, `__proto__`, `toLocaleString`) and every one reads `viewer(no-user)` with no stored user and `500(TypeError)` with one; so do the ARRAY ids `["constructor"]` and `["toString"]`; `prototype` and an unknown token read `401(null)` (controls); a real session reads `role=admin`; the sessions file was 249 bytes before and after and `lastActivity` reached no built-in. (ii) **Over HTTP** (`probe/http_probe.js`, `node backend/server.js` of the export on `127.0.0.1:10130` and `:10131`, `NODE_ENV=development`, fresh `DATA_DIR`/`HOME`, seeded through the export's own `JsonStorage`: zero-GUID Entra ids, `authEnforced` true, `firstRunComplete` true, `aiEnabled` true, `OLLAMA_ENDPOINT` at a loopback port where nothing listened; each server stopped by its pid; `lsof -nP -iTCP:10130-10139 -sTCP:LISTEN` 0 rows after): server **N** (no stored user): each of the 12 names and the JSON form `j%3A%5B%22constructor%22%5D` answered 200/200/200/403 on `/api/auth/check`/`/api/printers`/`/api/stats`/`/api/auth/users` and **200 on `/index.html`**, and POST `/api/chat` with `constructor` and a CSRF token answered **200** (model-free); `prototype` and an unknown token 401 `SESSION_EXPIRED` and 302 to `/login`; no cookie 401 `AUTH_REQUIRED`. Server **U** (an admin and a viewer stored, one session each): the 13 reserved forms answered 500 `AUTH_ERROR` on the four APIs and on POST `/api/chat`, and **302 to `/login` on `/index.html`** (requireAuth's catch redirects a page); the admin session 200 on `/api/auth/users`, the viewer 403; 66 `Authentication middleware error` log lines, each a TypeError at `jsonStorage.js:3978`.
- **Why (re-read by the drafter at source, `ed3b1aed`):** `getSession` (`backend/jsonStorage.js:4071`) reads `const session = sessions[sessionId];` (`:4073`), which returns the INHERITED built-in for these names; its `expiresAt` is undefined and `new Date(undefined) < new Date()` is false, so it never expires; requireAuth then calls `getAuthorizedUser(session.email)` with `undefined` (`server.js:2757`): an empty user list returns undefined and the request passes as role `viewer`; a stored user makes `email.toLowerCase()` throw (`jsonStorage.js:3978`), so 500. **A JSON cookie reaches it too:** cookie-parser 1.4.7 turns the value `j:["constructor"]` (sent percent-encoded) into the ARRAY `["constructor"]`, and `({})[["constructor"]]` is the inherited function (MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER with the project's own `cookie-parser` and `cookie` 0.7.2).
- **Reachable in the product (RELAYED from the gate, re-read by the drafter):** the enforce route (`server.js:3834`, `app.post('/api/auth/enforce'`) lets an installer enforce before any user exists (its admin gate reads `hasAnyAuthorizedUsers()` at `:3848`), and the first Entra sign-in adds its user (`server.js:3384`), so every deployment passes through "enforced, no stored user"; the same holds if the authorized-users file reads empty.
- **The fix shape (RD-999's own text, the commission, the gate's recommendation):** `getSession` returns a session only for an OWN entry of the store whose key equals a string cookie, and only when that entry is an object with a string `email` and an `expiresAt` that parses to a time; everything else is null, which every caller already treats as "no session". **No caller reads the session store by a request value except through the store's own methods** (MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER at `ed3b1aed`: `getSession(` callers are only `server.js:2709` (requireAuth), `:2871` (the .html guard), `:2945` (`/api/auth/check`), `:3075` (logout); all 14 `sessionsFile` lines are inside `jsonStorage.js`), so the fix lives in `getSession` alone and **`server.js` is not edited**.
- **A scratch CANDIDATE of exactly that shape (the B1648 drafter's candidate re-applied by program to the `ed3b1aed` file; never a project file) was measured by the drafter:** in-process 34 lookups null (the 12 names, `prototype`, an unknown token and three array ids, in both states), the real session unchanged (`role=admin`; `viewer(no-user)` with no stored user, as before), 249 bytes before and after; over HTTP on `:10132` (N) and `:10133` (U): every reserved form 401 `SESSION_EXPIRED` on the four APIs and on POST `/api/chat`, 302 to `/login` on `/index.html`, 0 `Authentication middleware error` lines, the admin and viewer sessions exactly as at BASE; local CodeQL on the candidate tree 33 rows = BASE's 33, 0 gone, 0 new. **It is evidence of shape, not your design:** you write and measure your own.
- **You cite the ruling as "the product owner's 2026-11-17 ruling"; you write no card id, person's name or decision-queue id in any commit, comment or file.** Plain words for the PR: a sign-in cookie whose value is the name of a built-in object property (or a JSON cookie that wraps one) is no longer taken for a session; with sign-in enforced it is refused like any unknown cookie, whether or not a user is stored. **No new user-facing sentence** (the refusal is the existing `SESSION_EXPIRED` answer, `server.js:2717`); **no route gate changed; no migration; nothing deployed.**

