## THE DESIGN (one part, one commit A and its new test file; then K)
**Property (the closed list's property first):** a value is a session only if it is a string that names an OWN entry of the stored sessions object, and that entry is a non-null object with a string `email` and an `expiresAt` for which `new Date(expiresAt).getTime()` is a number; for every such entry the answer, the expiry rule, the delete of an expired entry and the stored bytes are what they were at BASE; for every other value `getSession` returns null, writes nothing and logs nothing that carries the request value. **Any other shape: prove it meets the property or STOP.**
1. **PART 1 (commit A), `backend/jsonStorage.js` `getSession` only.** Print the method at BASE with `grep -n` first. Form: `if (typeof sessionId !== 'string' || !Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(sessions, sessionId)) return null;` before the lookup, then the shape check before the expiry test; the expiry branch, its delete and its warning stay exactly as they are. **Not** a null-prototype copy of the store per request (an O(n) copy on every request; `readFile` is shared by every store and stays untouched), **not** a list of reserved names (the list is 12 names on node 26 and is the engine's, not ours), **not** a change to `createSession`, `updateSessionActivity`, `deleteSession` or `readFile`. The comment names `RD-999` and the risk in words: "a cookie that names a built-in property was read as a session; with sign-in enforced and no stored user it passed as a viewer". A malformed own entry is refused, not deleted (no new write path). **If the reading at your base finds any reader of the session store by a request value outside `getSession`, `updateSessionActivity` and `deleteSession`, STOP with the lines** (the kit's claim is that there is none).
2. **The callers (read and prove, no edit).** For each `getSession(` caller (`server.js:2709`, `:2871`, `:2945`, `:3075` at drafting; re-print at your base): print the null branch it takes and what it answers. Prove by program that `server.js`'s blob at your head equals BASE's. Logout (`:3075`) calls `deleteSession(sessionToken)` whatever `getSession` answered: at `ed3b1aed` that is the rebuild without the key (harmless for an inherited name; RELAYED from the storage-family seat's STATUS); say so in READY.
3. **Cells (`__tests__/session-cookie-inherited-name-refused.test.js`, NEW; about 16 `test(` lines; the cell count comes from the jest JSON, never from `test(` lines).** In-process cells (a temp HOME and `DATA_DIR` set BEFORE the require, as `rd769` does; the store built on that directory; one real session made by `createSession`): (U1) every name of `Object.getOwnPropertyNames(Object.prototype)` at run time UNION the 12 the drafter printed, plus `prototype`: `getSession` returns null, the sessions file's bytes are unchanged, and no `lastActivity` property appears on `Object`, `Object.prototype` or `Object.prototype.toString` (clean up in a `finally`); (U2) non-string ids (`["constructor"]`, `["toString"]`, and an array holding the real token): null; (U3) the real session: deep-equal to the stored entry (pin); (U4) an expired real session: null and removed from the file (pin); (U5) an unknown string: null (pin); (U6) own entries with a numeric `email`, with `expiresAt` `"not a date"`, with no `expiresAt`, a `null` entry and a string entry: null, file bytes unchanged; (U7) source cell: the `getSession` method text holds an own-entry check before its first `sessions[` read (control at BASE: it does not). HTTP cells (two servers through `bootServer`, both in `beforeAll`, stopped and their directories removed in `afterAll`; both seeded with `aiEnabled` true and given `env: { OLLAMA_ENDPOINT: 'http://127.0.0.1:<port>' }` where `<port>` is a port of your band that `lsof` shows unbound (the gate's and the drafter's form; no model is called); server **N** seeded with zero-GUID Entra ids, `authEnforced` true and `firstRunComplete` true and NO user and NO session; server **U** seeded by `seedEnforced`): (H1) on N, for each of the 13 names and the JSON form `j%3A%5B%22constructor%22%5D` (percent-encoded `j:["constructor"]`): GET `/api/auth/check`, `/api/printers`, `/api/stats`, `/api/auth/users` each answer 401 with `code` `SESSION_EXPIRED`; (H2) the same on U (no 500); (H3) o